IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-s7-definitions-and-evidence`

-- ccc1-tests-s7-definitions-and-evidence.l4 -- tests for section 7(8) to (11) of the Criminal Code (Canada). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- Arguments are positional, in GIVEN order. Moments are hours on one clock.

§ `s 7(8) flight  (the act of flying or moving through the air)`
#ASSERT `s 7(8) flight` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the act of flying or moving through the air
#ASSERT `s 7(8) flight` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "flight means"

§ `s 7(8) deemed to be in flight  (moment; doors closed; door opened; forced landing; control restored)`
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 5 10 NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the doors were closed
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 9.99 10 NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- just before the doors were closed
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 10 10 NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the moment the doors were closed: "from the time when"
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 50 10 NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no door opened yet: the period has not ended
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 12 10 (JUST 20) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before any door was opened for disembarkation
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 19.99 10 (JUST 20) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- just before
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 20 10 (JUST 20) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the very moment the door was opened: the text does not say
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 20.01 10 (JUST 20) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the door was opened
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 25 10 (JUST 20) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- forced landing, control not yet restored: (b) has not happened, so the later of (a) and (b) has not come
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 25 10 (JUST 20) TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- forced landing: the later of the door (20) and control restored (30) is 30
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 30 10 (JUST 20) TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the moment control was restored
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 31 10 (JUST 20) TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after control was restored
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 35 10 (JUST 40) TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- forced landing: the later is the door (40), not the restoring (30)
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 40 10 (JUST 40) TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the end is 40
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 41 10 (JUST 40) TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after 40
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 25 10 (JUST 20) FALSE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no forced landing: paragraph (b) does not apply, so the end is the door (20)
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` 35 10 NOTHING TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- forced landing but no door opened yet: no end
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is in flight` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- flying: in flight, whatever the deeming says
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is in flight` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on the ground with the doors closed: deemed in flight
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is in flight` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 7(8) the aircraft is in flight` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the deeming did not answer

§ `s 7(9) in service  (moment; pre-flight preparation began; cancelled; landed; ceased to be in flight)`
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 0 1 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before pre-flight preparation began
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 1 1 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the moment pre-flight preparation began
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 100 1 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- nothing has ended it
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 4 1 (JUST 5) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): the flight is cancelled at 5, not yet
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 5 1 (JUST 5) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the moment of cancellation
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 6 1 (JUST 5) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the cancellation
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 20 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- landed at 10: twenty-four hours after is 34, later than ceasing to be in flight (12)
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 34 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) (JUST 12) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the end (b) is 34
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 35 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after 34
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 39 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ceasing to be in flight (40) is later than 34
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 40 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) (JUST 40) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the end (c) is 40
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 41 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after 40
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 34.4 1 NOTHING (JUST 10.5) (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- landed at 10.5: the end is 34.5
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 34.5 1 NOTHING (JUST 10.5) (JUST 12) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the end
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 34.6 1 NOTHING (JUST 10.5) (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 100 1 NOTHING (JUST 10) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- landed but (c) has not happened: the latest has not come
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 100 1 NOTHING NOTHING (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) happened but (b) has not
#ASSERT `s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` 100 1 (JUST 5) (JUST 10) (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a cancelled flight: the end is the cancellation (the other limbs do not occur)

§ `s 7(10)  (tendered in proceedings under this Act; purports to be issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs)`
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is admissible in evidence without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have signed it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- admissible
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is admissible in evidence without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have signed it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a certificate purporting to be the Minister's
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is admissible in evidence without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have signed it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in proceedings under this Act: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is proof of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- proof of the facts, no evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is proof of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of evidence to the contrary": there is evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is proof of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- facts not relevant to the question: not covered
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is proof of the facts it states` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in proceedings under this Act
#ASSERT `s 7(10) the certificate is proof of the facts it states` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the Minister's certificate

§ `s 7(11)  (purports to be issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs; what it states)`
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it` TRUE `s 7(11)(a) that at a certain time any state was engaged in an armed conflict against Canada or was allied with Canada in an armed conflict` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it` TRUE `s 7(11)(b) that at a certain time any convention, treaty or other international agreement was or was not in force and that Canada was or was not a party thereto` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it` TRUE `s 7(11)(c) that Canada agreed or did not agree to accept and apply the provisions of any convention, treaty or other international agreement in an armed conflict in which Canada was involved` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it` TRUE `s 7(11) something else` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another statement: not covered
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it` FALSE `s 7(11)(a) that at a certain time any state was engaged in an armed conflict against Canada or was allied with Canada in an armed conflict` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the Minister's certificate
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is proof of the facts so stated` TRUE `s 7(11)(a) that at a certain time any state was engaged in an armed conflict against Canada or was allied with Canada in an armed conflict` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): proof of the facts so stated
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is proof of the facts so stated` TRUE `s 7(11)(c) that Canada agreed or did not agree to accept and apply the provisions of any convention, treaty or other international agreement in an armed conflict in which Canada was involved` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is proof of the facts so stated` TRUE `s 7(11) something else` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another statement
#ASSERT `s 7(11) the certificate is proof of the facts so stated` FALSE `s 7(11)(b) that at a certain time any convention, treaty or other international agreement was or was not in force and that Canada was or was not a party thereto` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the Minister's certificate
